== Conditional mathematics, independently checked
The eight ChainDescent lemmas derive rational correction completeness from the norm-kernel description, Frobenius cube law on two-torsion, squared fixedness and equivariance. Averaging three conjugates gives a rational preimage. Full kernel transport proves half-choice independence and Frobenius-fixed output without assuming the desired beta evaluator.

The five FullGroupNorm lemmas derive both two-pair norms from individual dual identities and linearity, give recovery on the full annihilator, check exact inverse witnesses and prove retained-lift composition. Both original Lean gates and all 13 exact local bindings pass with zero trusted assumptions. Actual HLP varieties/polarizations, encoded fields, kernel/Frobenius identities, fixed-field descent and Picard/program correspondence remain explicit bridges. A finite panel and abstract module proof do not discharge those bridges.

== What the result advances
The project now has implemented complete maps for a fixed two-edge chain of genus 3 Jacobian models over the prime field, with full finite exceptional/cofactor validation and explicit recovery. The original fixed-source negatives and earlier full-cold-census failure are retained. The prospective next tasks are genuine 22 custody and exact replay CI, the norm-point reuse candidate, full setup/reuse primitive accounting, and separate original-prime/endpoint/factor-base investigations.

